*********** Record types ********* 
immutable data- value can't be changed over time. Ex- value type
mutable- value can be changed. Ex- reference type

When "record" type is used, it creates an immutable object. It's properties behave as readonly.
Ex:-
public record Person
{
    public string LastName { get; }
    public string FirstName { get; }

    public Person(string first, string last) => (FirstName, LastName) = (first, last);
}

is equivalent to

public class Person
{
    public readonly string LastName { get; }
    public readonly string FirstName { get; }

    public Person(string first, string last) => (FirstName, LastName) = (first, last);
}

"record" type is similar to type class. It supports inheritance.
public record Teacher : Person   //Person is of type record
{
}

"record" type can be sealed too.
public sealed record Student : Person
{
}

